        "q": "Why does Aquinas hold that the act of believing can be meritorious?",
        "options": [
          "Because it requires great intellectual effort",
          "Because it is an act of the intellect assenting to divine truth at the command of the will moved by grace, and so is subject to free will directed toward God",
          "Because belief is always accompanied by visible miracles",
          "Because it fulfills a legal precept of the Church"
        ],
        "correct": 1,
        "explanation": "Since meritorious acts proceed from free will moved by grace and referred to God, and the act of faith is precisely such an act of intellect commanded by a grace-moved will, believing can be meritorious."
